<report>
<title>Kendall's rank correlation</title>

<p><in>sample_1</in> vs. <in>sample_2</in><br />
Observations per sample = <in>obs</in><br />
Concordant pairs  =  <in>con</in><br />
Discordant pairs  =  <in>dis</in><br />
Tied pairs = <in>tie</in><br />
Kendall's score = <in>s</in>   (standard error = <inu>ses</inu>)<br />
Gamma = <inu>gam</inu></p>

<p>Kendall's <in>tb</in>  = <inu>tau</inu><br />
<ci>Approximate <in>pc</in>% CI = <inu>ll</inu> to <inu>ul</inu></ci></p>

<p><u>Approximate tests<in>adj</in></u></p>
<block name="smallsample">
<p><warn>Sample size too small for reliable inference from z, use exact test</warn></p>
</block>
<p>z = <inu>kz</inu><br />
<pval>Upper side <inp>p_u</inp></pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: concordance)<br />
<pval>Lower side <inp>p_l</inp></pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: discordance)<br />
<pval>Two sided <inp>p_2</inp></pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: dependence)</p>

<p>z (continuity corrected) = <inu>kzcc</inu><br />
<pval>Upper side <inp>p_ucc</inp></pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: concordance)<br />
<pval>Lower side <inp>p_lcc</inp></pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: discordance)<br />
<pval>Two sided <inp>p_2cc</inp></pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: dependence)</p>

<p><u>Exact test<in>adjexact</in></u><br />
<pval>Upper side <inp>p_uexact</inp></pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: concordance)<br />
<pval>Lower side <inp>p_lexact</inp></pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: discordance)<br />
<pval>Two sided <inp>p_2exact</inp></pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: dependence)</p>
</report>
